.TH koji-lag 1 2026-08-13 "sandogasa 0.19.4" "Sandogasa Manual"
.SH NAME
koji\-lag \- Quantify Koji build queue lag and per\-arch build\-time drag
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBkoji\-lag\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Quantify Koji build queue lag and per\-arch build\-time drag
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.SS koji-lag backfill
\fBkoji\-lag backfill\fR [\fB\-\-instance\fR] [\fB\-\-hub\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-since\fR] [\fB\-\-until\fR] [\fB\-\-days\fR] <\fB\-\-root\fR> [\fB\-\-reports\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-if\-exists\fR] [\fB\-\-page\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-sleep\-ms\fR] [\fB\-\-duty\-cycle\fR] [\fB\-\-retries\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-samples\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Sweep a long window a day at a time, collating as it goes
.TP
\fB\-\-instance\fR \fI<INSTANCE>\fR [default: fedora]
Known Koji instance (cbs, fedora, stream). Names the files
.TP
\fB\-\-hub\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
Explicit hub URL (overrides \-\-instance; https only)
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fI<YYYY\-MM\-DD>\fR
Window start date (UTC midnight, inclusive)
.TP
\fB\-\-until\fR \fI<YYYY\-MM\-DD>\fR
Window end date, inclusive
.TP
\fB\-\-days\fR \fI<N>\fR
Sweep the last N complete UTC days
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory to write the dataset tree into
.TP
\fB\-\-reports\-root\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Also write reports, into this directory tree
.TP
\fB\-\-if\-exists\fR \fI<WHAT>\fR [default: ask]
What to do when a day\*(Aqs dataset is already there
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
merge: Sweep again and fold the result into what is there
.IP \(bu 2
replace: Sweep again and write over it
.IP \(bu 2
ask: Ask, and merge when nobody can be asked
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-page\-size\fR \fI<PAGE_SIZE>\fR [default: 1000]
Tasks per listTasks page
.TP
\fB\-\-sleep\-ms\fR \fI<SLEEP_MS>\fR [default: 500]
Minimum pause between hub requests, in milliseconds
.TP
\fB\-\-duty\-cycle\fR \fI<PERCENT>\fR [default: 50]
Share of one connection to use, as a percentage
.TP
\fB\-\-retries\fR \fI<RETRIES>\fR [default: 3]
Retries per failed hub request
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-samples\fR \fI<MIN_SAMPLES>\fR [default: 5]
Withhold report stats below this sample count
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SS koji-lag fetch
\fBkoji\-lag fetch\fR [\fB\-\-instance\fR] [\fB\-\-hub\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-since\fR] [\fB\-\-until\fR] [\fB\-\-days\fR] [\fB\-\-owner\fR] [\fB\-\-package\fR] [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-inventory\fR] <\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR> [\fB\-\-page\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-sleep\-ms\fR] [\fB\-\-duty\-cycle\fR] [\fB\-\-retries\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-start\-below\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Sweep a Koji completion window into a local dataset
.TP
\fB\-\-instance\fR \fI<INSTANCE>\fR [default: fedora]
Known Koji instance (cbs, fedora, stream)
.TP
\fB\-\-hub\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
Explicit hub URL (overrides \-\-instance; https only)
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fI<YYYY\-MM\-DD>\fR
Window start date (UTC midnight, inclusive)
.TP
\fB\-\-until\fR \fI<YYYY\-MM\-DD>\fR
Window end date, inclusive (default: the last complete UTC day — the running day is never included implicitly)
.TP
\fB\-\-days\fR \fI<N>\fR
Sweep the last N complete UTC days
.TP
\fB\-\-owner\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Keep only builds submitted by this user
.TP
\fB\-\-package\fR \fI<NAME,...>\fR
Keep only these source packages (CSV or repeated)
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Keep only packages from these inventory files
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Dataset file to create or merge into
.TP
\fB\-\-page\-size\fR \fI<PAGE_SIZE>\fR [default: 1000]
Tasks per listTasks page
.TP
\fB\-\-sleep\-ms\fR \fI<SLEEP_MS>\fR [default: 500]
Minimum pause between hub requests, in milliseconds
.TP
\fB\-\-duty\-cycle\fR \fI<PERCENT>\fR [default: 50]
Share of one connection to use, as a percentage.

Each pause is scaled to how long the last request took, so a hub under load is asked less often and a hub that speeds up is asked more. 50 means pause as long as the request took; 100 paces by \-\-sleep\-ms alone.
.TP
\fB\-\-retries\fR \fI<RETRIES>\fR [default: 3]
Retries per failed hub request
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print progress to stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-start\-below\fR \fI<ID|FILE>\fR
Start below this build task id, or below the oldest in a dataset file.

A backfill knows the answer: a dataset covering a later window holds nothing this one wants, so the sweep can begin below the oldest build in it. Given a number, that id is used directly.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SS koji-lag merge
\fBkoji\-lag merge\fR <\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR> [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR> 
.PP
Union datasets collected independently into one
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Merged output file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
Dataset files to union
.SS koji-lag report
\fBkoji\-lag report\fR [\fB\-\-since\fR] [\fB\-\-until\fR] [\fB\-\-arch\fR] [\fB\-\-scratch\fR] [\fB\-\-official\fR] [\fB\-\-include\-failed\fR] [\fB\-\-out\fR] [\fB\-\-min\-samples\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR> 
.PP
Per\-arch queue\-wait / build\-time / bottleneck report
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fI<YYYY\-MM\-DD>\fR
Only tasks completing on/after this date (UTC midnight)
.TP
\fB\-\-until\fR \fI<YYYY\-MM\-DD>\fR
Only tasks completing on/before this date (UTC midnight)
.TP
\fB\-\-arch\fR \fI<ARCH,...>\fR
Restrict to these arches (CSV or repeated)
.TP
\fB\-\-scratch\fR
Only scratch builds
.TP
\fB\-\-official\fR
Only official (non\-scratch) builds
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-failed\fR
Include FAILED tasks in build\-time statistics
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Write report.txt and report.json into this directory.

Both forms in one pass, since a reader wants the table and a machine wants the fields, and running the report twice to get both would read the dataset twice. Without it the report goes to stdout, as text or as JSON with \-\-json.
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-samples\fR \fI<MIN_SAMPLES>\fR [default: 5]
Withhold human\-output stats below this sample count
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output machine\-readable JSON instead of tables
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
Dataset file(s) to report over (merged in memory)
.SS koji-lag reports
\fBkoji\-lag reports\fR <\fB\-\-root\fR> <\fB\-\-reports\-root\fR> [\fB\-\-min\-samples\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.PP
Render reports for every dataset in a tree, without fetching
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Dataset tree to read (as written by `backfill`)
.TP
\fB\-\-reports\-root\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory tree to write reports into
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-samples\fR \fI<MIN_SAMPLES>\fR [default: 5]
Withhold report stats below this sample count
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Re\-render reports that already exist.

Off by default, so re\-running after an interruption costs nothing; pass it after changing what a report says.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
